    <paragraph>Choose the Most Convenient Method to Solve a System of Linear Equations</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, decide whether it would be more convenient to solve the system of equations by substitution or elimination.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="64" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {- 3x - y = 8} \\ {6x + 2y = -16} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓑ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {4x + 3y = 2} \\ {20x + 15y = 10} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="65" has_solution="true">
